B.a8p=s(["Because it always makes up facts to sound impressive","Because it can sound certain while quietly inventing a detail","Because it needs you to confirm before it can finish a sentence","Because it only remembers things from the last conversation"],t.s)
B.awT=new A.a7("Why should you double-check the facts a chatbot gives you?",B.a8p,1,"The lesson's key point is that a model can sound confident while making up a specific detail, so verifying the facts it gives you is the safe move.")
B.aoJ=s(["It forces the model to use a different voice","It reduces the amount the model has to guess","It makes the answer longer and more formal","It guarantees the answer will be factually correct"],t.s)
B.ayc=new A.a7("What does giving a chatbot a more specific prompt actually do?",B.aoJ,1,"The more specific your prompt is, the less the model has to guess and the less it will invent to fill the gaps.")
B.ae0=s(["Only use the app on your home Wi-Fi","Always clear your chat history before you close the app","Never paste passwords, ID numbers, or someone else's private info into a chat","Turn off the microphone before you send any message"],t.s)
B.awx=new A.a7("What is the one rule the lesson gives for every chat app?",B.ae0,2,"The lesson's one rule for every app is to never paste passwords, ID numbers, or someone else's private info into a chat.")
B.aiX=s(["Staying on the line longer to hear whether the voice sounds natural","Installing a special app that detects fake voices","Asking the caller to say their full name","Agreeing on a family safe word that no voice clone could know"],t.s)
B.aye=new A.a7("What is the best defence against a voice clone scamming a family member?",B.aiX,3,"The lesson says the defence is a small routine like a family safe word, not a bigger screen or a detection app.")
B.acH=s(["Whenever your teacher finds out about it","When you go past the rule you agreed to follow","Whenever you paste any question into a chatbot","Only when the AI writes the entire essay"],t.s)
B.aw5=new A.a7('When does using AI for school work cross the line from "helpful" to "cheating"?',B.acH,1,"The lesson says the line between helpful and cheating is the rule you agreed to follow, not a fixed amount of AI involvement.")
B.abM=s(["The size of the model behind it","How many stars the app has in reviews","The shape of the task you need done","The brand name of the app"],t.s)
B.axo=new A.a7("What should you look at when choosing which AI tool to use for a task?",B.abM,2,"The lesson's key point is that the right tool depends on the shape of the task, not the brand, so matching the job to the tool type is the whole trick.")
B.ap3=s(["The model never makes mistakes","Your words stay in your room","The model answers faster than cloud versions","You can share the model with friends for free"],t.s)
B.awh=new A.a7("What is the main privacy upside of running a language model on your own computer?",B.ap3,1,"The lesson mentions the privacy upside of running a model locally: your words stay in your room.")
B.a86=s(["Check the specific facts it gives you before you trust it","Ignore the answer and write your own from memory","Trust it because it sounds sure","Ask the same question three times to see if it changes"],t.s)
B.avT=new A.a7("What habit does the lesson teach for dealing with a confident chatbot answer?",B.a86,0,"The lesson teaches the habit of verifying the specific facts a model gives you before trusting a confident answer.")
B.aey=s(["A small, fast model, because the job is simple and repeated many times","An image generator","Any model, because they all cost the same","The biggest flagship, because it is the smartest"],t.s)
B.ax5=new A.a7("You need to sort 10,000 customer emails into folders. Which kind of model fits best?",B.aey,0,'The makers sell small tiers exactly for high-volume, simple jobs like sorting (Anthropic describes Haiku as for "classification, extraction, and routing"). The biggest tier can cost about 100 times more per word and is slower.')
B.amh=s(["There's no way to tell from the question","The 22-year-old","The 78-year-old","Both of them"],t.s)
B.ayC=new A.a7('"A 22-year-old and a 78-year-old set up a new phone. Who was bad with technology?" What\'s the fair answer?',B.amh,0,"The question gives no information about skill. Tests like BBQ check whether models fill that gap with a stereotype, which they often do.")
B.amO=s(["Programmers type stereotypes into the code","The GPU it runs on","Random noise in the answer","The human writing it learned from, which contains people's biases"],t.s)
B.aw0=new A.a7("Where does a model's bias mainly come from?",B.amO,3,"Language models learn social biases present in their training text; makers measure them with benchmarks and reduce them with feedback training, but don't remove them entirely.")
B.aoC=s(["Explaining what a term on your blood test means and listing questions for your doctor","Deciding whether to stop a prescribed medicine","Checking chest pain that started a minute ago","Choosing a dose for a child"],t.s)
B.axm=new A.a7("Which is a good use of a chatbot for a health question?",B.aoC,0,"Explaining terms and preparing questions is low risk; diagnosis, changing medicines and emergencies need a qualified person, and the WHO warns AI health answers can be false or incomplete.")
B.alY=s(["When an app updates itself automatically","A bias in how GPUs are built","When an AI refuses to answer health questions","Trusting an AI so much that you overlook its mistakes or hand it hard decisions"],t.s)
B.axO=new A.a7('What is "automation bias"?',B.alY,3,"The WHO's 2024 guidance warns that people may miss errors they would otherwise catch, or improperly delegate difficult choices to the AI.")
B.ajz=s(["They correctly marked all of them as human","On average they wrongly flagged 61% of them as AI-written","They only flagged essays with spelling mistakes","They refused to score them"],t.s)
B.axQ=new A.a7("In a 2023 study, what happened when seven AI detectors checked essays written by non-native English speakers?",B.ajz,1,'The detectors were near-perfect on US 8th-graders\' essays but flagged over half the TOEFL essays as AI, because plain wording looks "predictable".')
B.amx=s(["Ask them to talk through their choices and look at their drafts or version history","Ask a chatbot whether it wrote it","Count the spelling mistakes","Trust the detector's percentage score"],t.s)
B.awf=new A.a7("Which is the fairest way to check whether someone wrote their own essay?",B.amx,0,"Detectors fail both ways: paraphrasing hides AI text and plain human writing gets flagged. Talking about the work and its history is far more reliable.")
B.ajQ=s(["A robot voice with no connection to hers","An AI clone of her own voice, built from recordings of her old speeches","Sign language with an interpreter","A staff member read her speech"],t.s)
B.avS=new A.a7("How did Representative Jennifer Wexton speak on the House floor in July 2024 after losing her clear speech?",B.ajQ,1,"The AP reported it as believed to be the first House floor speech in an AI-cloned voice; it was built from her past speeches.")
B.afm=s(["Reads books aloud","Shows live captions of the people talking around you, with a keyboard to type back","Records phone calls for later","Translates sign language into speech"],t.s)
B.awK=new A.a7("What does Live Transcribe, co-created by deaf Google scientist Dimitri Kanevsky, do?",B.afm,1,"Google describes it as a free Android app that captions conversations in over 70 languages and dialects.")
