B.am1=s(["It retrains the model after quantization","It uses second-order information to adjust remaining weights after each quantization step","It keeps the most important weights in full precision","It uses a much larger calibration dataset than other methods"],t.s)
B.axU=new A.a7("What is the core trick that keeps GPTQ accurate at 3-4 bits?",B.am1,1,"After quantizing each weight, GPTQ computes the optimal update for all remaining weights using the Hessian, compensating for the rounding error.")
B.aix=s(["It quantizes all rows in the same fixed order, cutting the computation by orders of magnitude","It runs on multiple GPUs simultaneously","It skips the layers with the largest weights","It uses a smaller calibration set than other methods"],t.s)
B.axt=new A.a7("Why does GPTQ finish in about 4 hours for a 175B model while prior methods would take weeks?",B.aix,0,"Using a fixed order means the Hessian update is done once per column instead of once per weight, reducing runtime from cubic to near-quadratic.")
