B.aiY=s(["A hard drive","HBM (High Bandwidth Memory)","A USB stick","CPU cache on the motherboard"],t.s)
B.axz=new A.a7("Which memory sits right next to an AI chip, stacked like a skyscraper?",B.aiY,1,"HBM chips are stacked on top of each other and placed beside the GPU, giving it terabytes per second of bandwidth.")
B.ag_=s(["They have bigger and faster fans","They do thousands of simple sums at once","They can store many more files","They connect to the internet faster"],t.s)
B.Gu=new A.a7("Why are GPUs better than CPUs at running AI?",B.ag_,1,"AI is mostly matrix multiplication: huge numbers of simple, independent math steps. That suits an army of GPU cores.")
B.alr=s(["140 MB","14 GB","140 GB","14 TB"],t.s)
B.avZ=new A.a7("Roughly how much memory does it take just to hold a 70-billion-parameter model at 16-bit precision?",B.alr,2,"2 bytes per parameter \xd7 70 billion = 140 GB, more than any single GPU holds.")
B.aj8=s(["How long data takes to start arriving","How much data can flow per second","How hot a chip runs","How many cores a chip has"],t.s)
B.ayF=new A.a7('What does "bandwidth" describe?',B.aj8,1,"Bandwidth is the width of the road: how many gigabytes per second can move. Latency is the wait before the first car arrives.")
B.abG=s(["Liquid is cheaper than air","Water carries far more heat than air","It makes them quieter for visitors","Water makes the chips compute more accurately"],t.s)
B.avU=new A.a7("Why are the newest AI racks liquid-cooled?",B.abG,1,"Water carries roughly 3,500\xd7 more heat than the same volume of air, and an NVL72 rack makes ~120 kW of heat.")
B.a98=s(["The building uses 50% extra power on top of the computers","The chips run at 150% speed","There are 1.5 GPUs per server","It uses 1.5 litres of water"],t.s)
B.axs=new A.a7("What does a PUE of 1.5 mean?",B.a98,0,"PUE = total power \xf7 computing power. 1.5 means for every watt of computing, half a watt goes to cooling and losses.")
B.abj=s(["0.01% of global electricity","About 1.5%","About 25%","More than half"],t.s)
B.Gr=new A.a7("About how much electricity did all the world's data centres use in 2024?",B.abj,1,"The IEA estimates ~415 TWh, about 1.5% of global electricity, and expects it to more than double, to ~945 TWh, by 2030.")
B.adS=s(["Wi-Fi","USB","NVLink","Bluetooth"],t.s)
B.axe=new A.a7("What links GPUs inside a server so they can share data super fast?",B.adS,2,"NVLink is a private express lane between GPUs: 900 GB/s per GPU on H100 and 1.8 TB/s on Blackwell.")
B.adW=s(["Square roots of every knob","Matrix multiplication","Sorting long lists of words","Counting letters in words"],t.s)
B.aya=new A.a7("Almost all the math inside an AI model is one operation. Which?",B.adW,1,"Every token passes through giant grids of knobs by matrix multiplication: about one multiply and one add per knob.")
B.aej=s(["They are more exact than FP32","Phones can only read those formats","They take less memory and are faster","They stop the model from making mistakes"],t.s)
B.ax0=new A.a7("Why do AI chips like using FP8 or FP4 numbers instead of FP32?",B.aej,3,"Fewer bits per number means a smaller model and faster math. Neural networks tolerate the rounding surprisingly well.")
B.acj=s(["About 1,000","About 10,000","About 100,000","About 10 million"],t.s)
B.axT=new A.a7("Roughly how many GPUs did xAI's first Colossus cluster in Memphis start with?",B.acj,2,"Around 100,000 H100 GPUs, installed in about 122 days in 2024.")
